Suppress warnings about undefined GNUMAKEFLAGS.

When make is run with --warn-undefined-variables and -R (--no-builtin-variables),
GNUMAKEFLAGS is undefined by undefine_default_variables(). However, decode_env_switches()
expands $(GNUMAKEFLAGS), which causes make to emit a spurious warning:
  warning: undefined variable 'GNUMAKEFLAGS'

Add GNUMAKEFLAGS to defined_vars in src/variable.c to treat it as defined
for the purposes of warn_undefined, matching the upstream fix.

Upstream bug: https://savannah.gnu.org/bugs/?64115
Upstream fix: https://git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/make.git/commit/?id=ebe0a1c9f1d1529a3f2c64d628686f500d460b0e

--- a/src/variable.c
+++ b/src/variable.c
@@ -1831,6 +1831,7 @@
   { STRING_SIZE_TUPLE ("MAKE_TERMOUT") },
   { STRING_SIZE_TUPLE ("MAKE_TERMERR") },
   { STRING_SIZE_TUPLE ("MAKEOVERRIDES") },
+  { STRING_SIZE_TUPLE ("GNUMAKEFLAGS") },
   { STRING_SIZE_TUPLE (".DEFAULT") },
   { STRING_SIZE_TUPLE ("-*-command-variables-*-") },
   { STRING_SIZE_TUPLE ("-*-eval-flags-*-") },
